              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners, petitioner argues that arbitrators derive their authority solely from the consent of the parties to the agreement."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 11,
                "start": 11
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners, if the contract expressly authorized class participation, petitioner would have no argument that the parties had not agreed to it."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 14,
                "start": 14
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners, petitioner points to AAA Rule\u202f3, which requires arbitrators to decide whether the arbitration clause permits class arbitration."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Waxman)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-96a930e090c5-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Mr. Waxman), according to Petitioner (Mr. Waxman), petitioner contends that the contract is not truly silent; there are arguments about its terms."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Waxman",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 60,
                "start": 60
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Waxman, petitioner notes that the contracts at issue are form contracts drafted by charterers and brokers, and they contain varied arbitration clauses."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MS. PILLARD",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
              "evidence_ids": [
